/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    A rabbit's text is inserted into a series outside it, through a second name made in the rabbit.

    Text is copied, never refused: to where the series itself lives, which the second name does not
    say (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, *Open*, closed 2026-11-25). */

Define words as a series of text.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define k as words.
    Define w as "ab" joined to "cd".
    Insert w into k.
Done.
Define junk as a series of text.
For each n in range 1 to 200, insert "junk {n}" into junk.
State words.
